WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.678
Every AI identity drifts once it
exists: a sponsor changes jobs,

2
00:00:04.678 --> 00:00:08.238
a developer adds a secret,
an agent gets a new tool.

3
00:00:08.238 --> 00:00:13.237
M twenty-five twenty-one asks monitoring
of high-impact AI to detect changes to a

4
00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:18.388
system after deployment, and the identity
logs are where those changes land first.

5
00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:23.770
So the program collects every AI identity's
sign-ins, audit events and risk signals,

6
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.383
and ties each one to its identity record,

7
00:00:26.383 --> 00:00:30.262
because nothing in a service
principal's sign-in says it's AI.

8
00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:32.425
Discovery is a standing input.

9
00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:37.430
Shadow AI shows up in four places:
services people use, apps holding

10
00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:43.163
consented access, agents on endpoints,
and AI built in the agency's own clouds.

11
00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:46.088
Anything found without
a record is a finding.

12
00:00:46.088 --> 00:00:49.374
An agentic AI system with
no governed identity

13
00:00:49.374 --> 00:00:52.324
is the finding this
book exists to prevent.

14
00:00:52.324 --> 00:00:55.781
It's high priority: it halts,
alerts a named person,

15
00:00:55.781 --> 00:00:58.200
and is never fixed automatically.

16
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.320
And A P I keys stay
invisible to all of it.
